# Shrugs Manaspoon — guest burglar and demolition specialist

**Name:** Working **Shrugs Manaspoon / Man-a-Spoon**, surname **ASR-provisional**, pending cast introduction/audio; **performed by Brian Dunaway** in [Delvers S2E04](../../episodes/S2E04.md). **Not** a Darkest Delvers permanent guild recruit at this cutoff.

## Introduction and appearance

In the cart of the Cloven Brotherhood at midnight, Shrugs appears as a **lanky wood elf with dark hair and copper-toned skin**, quiet and neat but not ostentatious. He wears gloves and a cloak and prefers avoiding attention or dirty hands. Strings of **dynamite are bound around his waist** under his clothes, with small bombs near his chest. He carries a **Flame Tongue rapier** with a flame-igniting mechanism and can pick locks with startling quickness. His signature shrug of raised shoulders and open palms is a genuine part of his demeanor.[^introduction]

## The Withers Estate infiltration

Cassius's alias **Suis Sac** has drawn the Cloven Brotherhood to Withers's riches, with Shrugs as its demolition expert and Allspice driving escape. Shrugs accepts **one mission Bag of Holding**, while Koh's **Psychic Whispers** makes them part of the same mental communications net. Krandal uses a **Scroll of Silence**, allowing Shrugs to **blow through the first alarm-wired underground oak door with two sticks of dynamite**. He later picks a second locked door with a **natural twenty, 26 total**, without setting off its bells. He notices the dried kuo-toa corpse, privately cuts off **a mummified toe**, and later takes a **wind-up wooden music box whose internal record/cylinder is missing**. He tries a sip of wine called **Blue Eyes**, returning the bottle rather than stealing it.[^cellar]

When elemental guardians block the route, Shrugs tosses dynamite at **Fern the fire elemental**, damaging the guardian and incidentally wounding Koh, later ignites his **Flame Tongue rapier** against the water elemental, and ends up engulfed by that creature. During the air elemental's violent gusts, Shrugs becomes **unconscious at 0 HP**; Krandal's **Preserve Life** restores him to consciousness and the guest survives. A coat-closet riddle sends Shrugs upstairs. His unsuccessful search ends in his carrying a gigantic pile of coats, which a **servant sees**, shouting that thieves and a **“coat monster”** have entered the mansion. Koh eventually finds the key among those coats.[^battles]

In the lower vault Shrugs collects a **mirror, painting and book filled with honey** into his mission Bag of Holding. He lights **another dynamite charge** under Krandal's second **Silence** to open the jewel vault; the transcript says **six sticks planted** but later **four exploded**, and the actual consumption needs verification. Shrugs and Koh gather enormous quantities of unidentified, unappraised gems and other objects before **all four adventurers escape in Allspice's cart**. At cutoff **no payout or guild/Cassius debrief**, no clear division of valuables, and no continuing guest membership is played.[^escape]

## Current status

Shrugs **actually participates in and survives the completed Withers Estate burglary**, including a period unconscious during the air-guardian battle from which **Krandal revives him**. He **holds one mission-provided Bag of Holding containing assorted treasures and gems**, along with the **incomplete music box** and **mummified kuo-toa toe**; neither bag's final contents, reward share nor return is reconciled. His **Flame Tongue rapier** and remaining dynamite are **not confirmed surrendered or lost**, with final count unclear. A servant saw him disguised as a pile of coats, so the heist was **not wholly unnoticed**. **Brian Dunaway's later return, if any, is outside S2E04.**[^escape]

[^introduction]: [Delvers S2E04](../../episodes/S2E04.md), ~00:00–00:16. Introduction/descriptive appearance provided by Brian Dunaway; **Manaspoon** surname phonetic in both exports. Costume and gear are played.
[^cellar]: [S2E04](../../episodes/S2E04.md), ~00:19–00:35, ~00:40–00:55, ~01:14–01:25. Two-stick first dynamite breach, successful trap cut/pick, physical dried kuo-toa toe/music box, wine sampled/returned.
[^battles]: [S2E04](../../episodes/S2E04.md), ~01:17–02:52. Fire collateral to Koh, water engulfment, air **unconscious/revived**, failed coat search and servant's direct witness. No claim guest ever officially joined guild.
[^escape]: [S2E04](../../episodes/S2E04.md), ~02:50–03:03. Miscount **six planted / four exploded** final charge, mirror/painting/honey-book bagged, gems bagged, cart escape completed; **no payments or appraisal**.
